        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "74aea86f-5226-5073-9487-88e9459f3519",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Roles: singer-songwriters, guitarists, vocalists, record producers\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945 and died on June 29, 1979.\n- Ian Hunter is a British singer-songwriter.\n- Lowell George was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from its inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Ian Hunter also served as lead singer of Mott the Hoople during the band's 2009 and 2013 reunions.",
